# No line-ending conversion, anywhere.
#
# Git rewrites line endings on checkout for files it decides are text, and on Windows that is the
# default. For most projects that is a convenience. Here it silently changes bytes that are the
# contract: the two signed catalogs are embedded with `include_bytes!` and checked against a
# compiled-in Ed25519 key, so a checkout that turns their newlines into carriage-return pairs
# produces a binary whose own manifest cannot verify. That was the state of every Windows checkout of
# this repository until this file existed, and it is not a test-only fault: a launcher built there
# could not have resolved an index pin or an addon component at all.
#
# The rule is global rather than a list of the artifacts that have bitten us, because the list is not
# knowable in advance. Golden trees, recorded fixtures, patch corpora and signed manifests are all
# byte-exact by design, and a project whose whole claim is byte-identity to another implementation
# should not have a checkout step that edits its files. Working with LF everywhere costs nothing:
# every toolchain this repository uses reads it on every platform.
* -text
